Q: Angular Signal Forms with Resources A: <p>I believe using a <code>linkedSignal</code> would be ideal when combining <strong>Signal Resources</strong> with <strong>Signal Forms</strong>:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>private readonly tenantService = inject(TenantService);

private readonly id = signal('1');
private readonly tenantResource = resource({
  params: () =&gt; this.id(),
  loader: ({ params }) =&gt; this.tenantService.getById(params),
});

protected readonly tenant = linkedSignal(() =&gt;
  this.tenantResource.hasValue()
    ? this.tenantResource.value()
    : &lt;Tenant&gt;{ name: '' }
);
protected readonly tenantForm = form(this.tenant);
</code></pre>
<p>Full working example on <a href="https://stackblitz.com/edit/stackblitz-starters-qdzw49le?file=src%2Fmain.ts" rel="nofollow noreferrer">StackBlitz</a></p>

Q: Reading wide character strings from stdin A: <p>Primarily, the return value of <code>wscanf()</code> is the number of items scanned, not <code>EOF</code>.  You therefore want to scan until it returns 0.</p>
<p>You are reading from an uninitialized array.  You want to declare it,</p>
<pre><code>wchar_t word [ MAX_WORD_LENGTH ] = {};
</code></pre>
<p>Or you might as well declare this <code>static</code>, since your <code>main()</code> does not need to be re-entrant.</p>
<p>You want to set your locale and console’s code page before you do any input and output:</p>
<pre><code>if (!setlocale( LC_ALL, &quot;.utf-8&quot; )) { // The user's language and settings, in UTF-8.
     // Report error here.
}

if (!SetConsoleCP(CP_UTF8)) {
     // Report error here.
}

if (!SetConsoleOutputCP(CP_UTF8)) {
     // Report error here.
}
</code></pre>
<p>Or if you want to do input and output in UTF-16, that code page is <code>1200</code> for little-endian UTF-16 or <code>1201</code> for big-endian UTF-16.</p>
<p>You should always, <em>always</em>, <em><strong>always</strong></em> check for buffer overruns in C!  Add a buffer-size specifier to the <code>%*s</code> format specifier.</p>

Q: Fetching user data (Next.js + Supabase) A: <p>you should use middleware.ts for this things.</p>
<p>middleware.ts can do authentication control for pages you can set this things... for example:</p>
<pre><code>import { NextResponse } from &quot;next/server&quot;;
import type { NextRequest } from &quot;next/server&quot;;
import { createMiddlewareClient } from &quot;@supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs&quot;;

// Routes that require authentication
const protectedRoutes = [&quot;/dashboard&quot;, &quot;/admin&quot;, &quot;/profile&quot;];

export async function middleware(req: NextRequest) {
  // Create a response object (required for cookie handling)
  const res = NextResponse.next();

  // Create Supabase client compatible with Next.js middleware
  const supabase = createMiddlewareClient({ req, res });

  // Get the currently authenticated user (if any)
  const {
    data: { user },
  } = await supabase.auth.getUser();

  // Current request path
  const pathname = req.nextUrl.pathname;

  // Check if the requested path is protected
  const isProtectedRoute = protectedRoutes.some((route) =&gt;
    pathname.startsWith(route)
  );

  // If user is not authenticated and route is protected → redirect to login
  if (!user &amp;&amp; isProtectedRoute) {
    const loginUrl = new URL(&quot;/login&quot;, req.url);
    return NextResponse.redirect(loginUrl);
  }

  // Allow the request to continue
  return res;
}

// Define which routes the middleware should run on
export const config = {
  matcher: [&quot;/dashboard/:path*&quot;, &quot;/admin/:path*&quot;, &quot;/profile/:path*&quot;],
};
</code></pre>
